language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Maximum clique: choose the largest set of vertices of a graph in which every two chosen vertices are adjacent.
given n : int(1..)
$ adj[i,j] = 1 when vertices i and j are joined by an edge
given adj : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int(0..1)
$ c[i] is true when vertex i is in the clique
find c : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of bool
branching on [c]
maximising (sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(c[i]))
such that
$ two distinct vertices both in the clique must be joined by an edge
forAll i : int(1..n) . forAll j : int(1..n) . ((i != j /\ c[i] /\ c[j]) -> adj[i,j] = 1)
